n the routine use  cases running clinical trials with a  signature of biomarkers already narrowed  down so by design lower level of  multiplexing and a higher level of  samples to run with our business model  at its core relies on the  commercialization of these high quality  reagents there are three ways we  interact with our customers for the  upcoming year in 2018 we will launch a  portfolio of kits that will fully be  compatible with the wide range of  instrumentation out of Staters and  multispectral imaging scanners these  kids will be designed in such a way that  they will seamlessly integrate with  these existing workflows as of today  we're engaging with customers through  FIFA services where we receive samples  that will run on behalf of our customer  either on standard panels that have  already been validated internally or  custom panels based on specific requests  made by our customers in some selected  few cases we also extend the service in  a further partnership where we can  explore further ways to deeply connect  with our customer base  in a nutshell our value proposition  touches on HIGH multiplexing institute  the ability to record an unlimited  number of markers on single tissue  slides while keeping the spatial  information intact and we do so while  fully preserving the antigenicity and  integrity of the samples our reagent  platform will be widely applicable to  the full range of instrumentation other  Stanners imaging scanners and is as of  today applicable to any FFP tissue slide  our technology is also amenable to very  high throughput by virtue of the fact  that we rely as you will see on a single  staining step and single amplification  step regardless of the number of markers  you would be looking at on these single  tissue slides and of course the kids  that we will launch in 2018 will be  meant to be fully plug-and-play easy to  use seamlessly integrated in existing  workflows and instruments  without further ado let's dive into the  data that we are able to generate with  our in-situ Plex reagents the images  that you're looking at were captured  from a tonsil tissue slide looking at a  five Plex panel composed of Dappy c d3  t 67p d1 and cytokeratin the image on  the left hand side is a 20x  magnification zoomed out portion of that  tonsil tissue the image on the right  hand side is a zoomed in section of one  of the lymph node of the tonsil  going into the nuts and bolts of our  Institute Lex platform our technology  relies on DNA mediated fluorescence we  introduce an intermediate bridge  composed of two complimentary DNA  strands between the antibody and the  label one strand the barcode is  covalently attached to the FC domain of  the antibody it's complementary form the  label to a floor for our technology's  robustness is guaranteed by three  building blocks the inner conjugation  that ties into the specificity of the  platform where we guarantee that the act  of conjugation of our bar codes to the  antibody does not impair the underlying  performance of that antibody and also in  the way we design pairs of barcodes and  label we make sure that there's no cross  reactivity between any given two pairs  DNA amplification ties to the  sensitivity of our platform whereby we  can elongate and extend the length of  any given barcode to create a polymer on  top of these barcodes a bit like  branches of a Christmas tree on which  you'll be able to attach many more  labels themselves conjugated to to floor  force as a result you increase the ratio  of barcodes per antibody and therefore  the amount of floor force that can  hybridize through the label onto the  antibody what guarantees the  reversibility of our platform is what we  call DNA exchange the act of D  hybridizing at will the labels from  their barcodes  at any point in time  so how did we generate the five kliks  images that you saw before  after conjugating five different  barcodes to the antibody specific to the  markers of interest w